      <div class="rx-photo">{% image "hiw2-who-senior-couple-bw.jpg", "An older couple, representing a surviving partner moving home" %}<div class="rx-tag">from<strong>&pound;{{ (site.packages | findByKey("bronze")).price | gbp }}</strong>packing and removals</div></div>
      <div class="rx-copy">
        <span class="gd-eyebrow" style="text-align:left">After a bereavement</span>
        <h2>Help with the home, <em>at the family&rsquo;s pace</em></h2>
        <p class="rx-sub">Dealing with a home after a death is hard enough without a deadline. Probate and legal steps are for the executor and their solicitor. The practical work of sorting, packing and moving is where we can take the weight off the family.</p>
        <ul class="rx-points"><li><i class="fas fa-clipboard-list" aria-hidden="true"></i><h3>Sorting with the family</h3><p>Room by room, with the executor and family deciding what is kept, sold, donated or passed on. Nothing goes without agreement.</p></li><li><i class="fas fa-heart" aria-hidden="true"></i><h3>Care with personal things</h3><p>Photographs, letters, jewellery and papers are set aside to decide on properly, not swept up in a bulk clear-out.</p></li><li><i class="fas fa-box-open" aria-hidden="true"></i><h3>Packing and moving</h3><p>What is being kept is packed, labelled and moved by DBS-checked staff, insured against loss or damage in transit.</p></li><li><i class="fas fa-home" aria-hidden="true"></i><h3>A surviving partner&rsquo;s move</h3><p>If a husband, wife or partner needs to downsize or move closer to family, we can run that move with a dedicated coordinator.</p></li></ul>
        <p class="rx-where">What is included depends on the package. Any legal, probate or tax question should go to the estate&rsquo;s solicitor or to GOV.UK.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="gd-sec grey">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="gd-head"><span class="gd-eyebrow">Who does what</span><h2>Where does Chayce fit, and <em>where does it not?</em></h2></div>
    <div class="gd-rows">
      <div class="gd-row"><h3>Executor and solicitor</h3><p>Handle probate, the legal duties around the estate and the decisions about who gets what. Chayce does not give legal, tax or probate advice.</p></div>
      <div class="gd-row"><h3>House-clearance firm</h3><p>Empties a property for disposal or sale. Chayce does not do this: we sort, pack and move what the family chooses to keep.</p></div>
      <div class="gd-row"><h3>Chayce</h3><p>Helps the family sort and decide, packs and moves belongings, and moves a surviving partner or relative. Nothing goes without the family&rsquo;s agreement.</p></div>
      <div class="gd-row"><h3>Before you move anything</h3><p>Check with the executor or solicitor before items are given away, sold or removed from the property, so nothing is disposed of too early. Our guide to <a href="/blog/moving-after-probate-clearing-a-loved-ones-home/">moving after probate and clearing a loved one&rsquo;s home</a> sets this out.</p></div>
    </div>
